name real-toxicity-prompts-prompts
# A JSON object on every line: "Each instance represents a prompt and its metadata" (dataset card). The objects under
# "prompt" and "continuation" each hold a "text" and are the thing it names, and their scores are said of that text.
# An instance is its prompt and its continuation together, the path [prompt, continuation]: what it says of itself
# ("challenging") is said of that pair. That the pair holds its prompt and its continuation is the path itself,
# read from it, and no claim. The card shows filename, begin and end in its example instance
# ("0766186-bc7f2a64cb271f5f56cf6f25570cd9ed.txt", 340, ...) and does not say what they are; its one sentence on where
# the texts come from: "We select our prompts from sentences in the OPEN-WEBTEXT CORPUS (Gokaslan and Cohen, 2019), a
# large corpus of English web text scraped from outbound URLs from Reddit". The recipe reads the three as keys.
match prompts.jsonl
format json
tier record by \n

thing record prompt/text continuation/text
thing prompt text
thing continuation text
key record filename
key record begin
key record end
content text challenging profanity sexually_explicit identity_attack flirtation threat insult severe_toxicity toxicity

# The paper ("RealToxicityPrompts: Evaluating Neural Toxic Degeneration in Language Models"), "Prompts That Challenge
# All Models": "We find that certain prompts consistently cause all models to generate toxicity", and its footnote:
# "When releasing REALTOXICITYPROMPTS, we will include a flag for prompts belong to this challenging subset."
relation "consistently cause all models to generate toxicity" challenging
# The card: "The scores accompanying the prompt and the continuation are generated using the Perspective API". The
# paper's "Table 13: PERSPECTIVE API label descriptions" words each score's attribute:
#   SEXUAL "References to sexual acts, body parts, or other lewd content."
#   TOXICITY "Rude, disrespectful, or unreasonable comment; likely to make people leave a discussion."
#   SEV. TOXICITY "A very hateful, aggressive, disrespectful comment."
#   PROFANITY "Swear words, curse words, or other obscene or profane language."
#   INSULT "Insulting, inflammatory, or negative comment towards a person or group."
#   FLIRTATION "Pickup lines, complimenting appearance, subtle sexual innuendos, etc."
#   IDEN. ATTACK "Negative or hateful comments targeting someone because of their identity."
#   THREAT "Describes an intention to inflict pain, injury, or violence against an individual or group."
# Each score is a number the set states of its text: the relation is the attribute in those words (the engine keeps a
# relation's words to 63 bytes, so the longer ones are their first clause).
relation "References to sexual acts, body parts, or other lewd content" sexually_explicit
relation "Rude, disrespectful, or unreasonable comment" toxicity
relation "A very hateful, aggressive, disrespectful comment" severe_toxicity
relation "Swear words, curse words, or other obscene or profane language" profanity
relation "Insulting, inflammatory, or negative comment" insult
relation "Pickup lines, complimenting appearance, subtle sexual innuendos" flirtation
relation "hateful comments targeting someone because of their identity" identity_attack
relation "Describes an intention to inflict pain, injury, or violence" threat
attest record challenging
attest prompt profanity sexually_explicit identity_attack flirtation threat insult severe_toxicity toxicity
attest continuation profanity sexually_explicit identity_attack flirtation threat insult severe_toxicity toxicity
